+# The privacy page: where every sentence comes from
+
+**Written:** 4 October 2026, for the page `pages/privacy.html` (it is built into `privacy.html`). It is added by the optional patch `patches/optional/privacy-page.patch`.
+
+**This is not legal advice, and the page is not a legal promise.** It says what the website's own code does, in plain words. It does not use the words of any privacy law and it does not claim that the farm follows one. If the farm wants the page read against the law, ask an adviser to read it. Give the adviser this document too.
+
+## In short
+
+- **Every sentence on the page is in the table below**, with the file or the test that shows it is true. `tests/privacy-page.test.mjs` fails when a sentence on the page is not in this document.
+- **The page says only what the code does.** It does not say what the hosting company, the map services, Mailchimp or an analytics company do with their own records. It says that they keep their own.
+- **Two settings change what is true.** If the farm turns on a visit counter, the page switches itself to the second set of sentences (rows P05 to P06 and P25 to P28). If the farm connects the Mailchimp form, the page is still true: its sentences cover both ways.
+- **The translations need a native reader.** Spanish, Hindi, Chinese and Vietnamese were written by Claude, not by a native speaker. Use `python3 tools/review_sheet.py` to make the sheets for them.
+
+## What the page leaves out on purpose
+
+- **The season and the game scores are not kept.** Some notes about this site say the season or the badges are saved in the browser. The code and the `privacy` test show they are not: only three notes are kept (rows P07 to P10). The page does not mention them as saved.
+- **The hosting company is not named.** The farm has not chosen one in the code. The page says "a hosting company" and that it keeps its own records (row P30).
+- **The live week feed is not covered.** `week.feed` in `js/content.js` is empty. If the farm sets it, the home page asks another site each time it opens. Add a sentence to the page first. `tests/privacy-page.test.mjs` fails until the setting is empty again or the page is changed.
+- **What the outside companies do with their records is not on the page.** The fact sheet `docs/WHAT_THE_SITE_STORES.md` (section 8) says what could be read about them and what could not.
+
+## When to check the page again
+
+Check it (run `node tests/run-all.mjs privacy privacy-page analytics`) and change it when any of these changes:
+
+- a new storage key, a cookie, or a new outside site (the `privacy` test fails first);
+- `analytics` in `js/content.js` (the page switches itself, but read the second set of sentences);
+- the Mailchimp form (`signup`), the drive time box, or the calendar buttons;
+- the hosting company or its settings (for example, a host that adds its own cookies);
+- the contact email in the footer.
+
+Change `docs/WHAT_THE_SITE_STORES.md` in the same change. It is the longer fact sheet that this page is made from.
+
+## The table
+
+Each row has a number, the sentence as the page says it, where the code shows it, and how it was checked. "The `privacy` test" means `tests/privacy.test.mjs`. The page says "the farm" where the code is the farm's own.
