@@ -0,0 +1,171 @@
+---
+title: Privacy at Wise Acres | Wise Acres Organic Farm
+description: What the Wise Acres website keeps on your device, when it sends anything to other sites, and who to ask. Plain words, written on 4 October 2026.
+crumb: Privacy
+---
+    <section class="page-hero" aria-labelledby="pg-h">
+      <div class="wrap page-hero-inner">
+        <div class="page-hero-copy">
+          <p class="hand hero-kicker">Your privacy</p>
+          <h1 id="pg-h">What this website keeps and shares</h1>
+          <p class="lead">This page says, in plain words, what the Wise Acres website does with your information. It is not legal advice.</p>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="section" id="short" aria-labelledby="short-h">
+      <div class="wrap">
+        <header class="section-head">
+          <p class="hand eyebrow">In a few words</p>
+          <h2 id="short-h">The short version</h2>
+        </header>
+        <ul class="fact-grid">
+          <li class="fact-card c-mint">
+            <h3>No accounts, no ads</h3>
+            <p>You do not need an account. The website shows no ads, and its own code sets no cookies.</p>
+          </li>
+          <li class="fact-card c-sky">
+            <h3>Notes on your device</h3>
+            <p>If you pick a language or tick the First-visit checklist, your browser keeps a small note of it.</p>
+          </li>
+          <li class="fact-card c-sun">
+            <h3>Other sites, only on request</h3>
+            <p>Drive time, the email list and Google Calendar send information to other sites, and only when you press their button.</p>
+          </li>
+          <li class="fact-card c-pink" data-analytics="off">
+            <h3>No visit counter</h3>
+            <p>The website&rsquo;s own code does not count or track your visit.</p>
+          </li>
+          <li class="fact-card c-pink" data-analytics="on" hidden>
+            <h3>A visit counter is on</h3>
+            <p>The farm counts visits with a service from another company. See the visit counter section below.</p>
+          </li>
+        </ul>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="section section-tint" id="device" aria-labelledby="device-h">
+      <div class="wrap two-col">
+        <div>
+          <header class="col-head">
+            <p class="hand eyebrow">On your device</p>
+            <h2 id="device-h">What your browser keeps</h2>
+          </header>
+          <p class="lead">The website keeps three small notes in your browser, and only after you choose something. Just reading the pages keeps nothing.</p>
+          <ul class="ticks ticks-lg">
+            <li>Language: the code of the language you picked (for example es), so your next visit opens in it</li>
+            <li>No thanks: a note that you said no to the language question, so it is not asked again</li>
+            <li>Checklist: which boxes you ticked in the First-visit checklist</li>
+          </ul>
+        </div>
+        <div>
+          <p>These notes stay on your device until you clear this site&rsquo;s data in your browser. They have no end date. The website does not send them to the farm.</p>
+          <p>Some things live only while the page is open: game scores, the place open on the map, and anything you type in a box. They are gone when you close or reload the page.</p>
+          <p>Nothing else is kept: no cookies from the website, no session storage, no database and no background program.</p>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="section" id="sent" aria-labelledby="sent-h">
+      <div class="wrap">
+        <header class="section-head">
+          <p class="hand eyebrow">Only when you press a button</p>
+          <h2 id="sent-h">When information goes to another site</h2>
+          <p class="lead">Three features send your information to other sites, and only after you press their button.</p>
+        </header>
+        <ul class="fact-grid fact-grid-3">
+          <li class="fact-card">
+            <h3>Drive time</h3>
+            <p>You type an address and press Get drive time. The address goes to OpenStreetMap&rsquo;s free address search.</p>
+            <p>Two map points go to the free OSRM route server: the place found for your address, and the place you chose to drive to. The words you typed do not.</p>
+            <p>The website does not keep the address. The two services may keep a record of the request.</p>
+            <p>Under the answer is a button for Google Maps. Your address goes to Google only if you press it.</p>
+            <p>Your browser may offer to fill in or remember the address. That is your browser&rsquo;s feature.</p>
+          </li>
+          <li class="fact-card">
+            <h3>Email list</h3>
+            <p>If you join, your email address goes to Mailchimp, the company that sends the farm&rsquo;s emails. The website does not send it before you press the button.</p>
+            <p>When the farm uses the form on the home page, the topics you tick go with your email address. So does your language, if the farm set that up. The form tells you.</p>
+          </li>
+          <li class="fact-card">
+            <h3>Add to Google Calendar</h3>
+            <p>Google Calendar opens in a new tab with the farm&rsquo;s opening times and the Bookeo link. Your name and email are not sent.</p>
+            <p>The other calendar button makes a file on your device and sends nothing.</p>
+          </li>
+        </ul>
+        <p>Other buttons and links take you to another site when you tap them. Examples are Bookeo for reservations, Square for pizza pre-orders, Google Maps, Apple Maps, Waze, Instagram, Facebook and Google Forms for school tours. After that, the other site&rsquo;s own rules apply. Email and phone links open your own email program or phone.</p>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="section section-tint" id="counter" aria-labelledby="counter-h">
+      <div class="wrap">
+        <header class="section-head">
+          <p class="hand eyebrow">Counting visits</p>
+          <h2 id="counter-h">Visit counter</h2>
+        </header>
+        <div data-analytics="off">
+          <p>No visit counter is switched on. The website&rsquo;s own code does not count or track your visit.</p>
+        </div>
+        <div data-analytics="on" hidden>
+          <p>The farm has switched on a visit counter, run by another company. It learns which pages are opened. Depending on the counter, it also learns which sections and buttons are used, and which language and season you pick.</p>
+          <p>The counter is never told what you type. It is not loaded at all if your browser asks sites not to track you (Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control).</p>
+          <p>The counter&rsquo;s own script runs on your device. That company decides what else it records, so read its own privacy page.</p>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="section" id="not" aria-labelledby="not-h">
+      <div class="wrap two-col">
+        <div>
+          <header class="col-head">
+            <p class="hand eyebrow">What the farm does not do</p>
+            <h2 id="not-h">Things you will not find here</h2>
+          </header>
+          <ul class="ticks ticks-lg">
+            <li>No accounts, logins or passwords</li>
+            <li>No ads, and no cookies set by the website&rsquo;s own code</li>
+            <li>No fonts, pictures, videos, embedded maps or social posts loaded from other sites</li>
+            <li>No use of your location, camera or microphone</li>
+            <li>No place to upload a photo or a file</li>
+            <li>Nothing you type is kept by the website</li>
+          </ul>
+        </div>
+        <div>
+          <p>The only two boxes where you can type are the email box and the address box for drive time. Neither asks for a name, an age or a photo.</p>
+          <p class="fine">The school tour sign-up is a Google Form on Google&rsquo;s own site. What it asks for is set in Google Forms, not on this website.</p>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="section section-tint" id="others" aria-labelledby="others-h">
+      <div class="wrap">
+        <header class="section-head">
+          <p class="hand eyebrow">Who else sees your visit</p>
+          <h2 id="others-h">Records kept by other companies</h2>
+        </header>
+        <p>Like any website, this one is served by a hosting company. Each time a page loads, that company receives your internet address (IP address) and your browser type, and it keeps its own records.</p>
+        <p>The same is true for the map services, Mailchimp and any site you reach by tapping a link. Each has its own rules for what it keeps. Ask them, or read their privacy pages.</p>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="section" id="clear" aria-labelledby="clear-h">
+      <div class="wrap">
+        <header class="section-head">
+          <p class="hand eyebrow">Your choices</p>
+          <h2 id="clear-h">How to clear what is kept</h2>
+        </header>
+        <p>To remove the notes the website keeps, clear this site&rsquo;s data in your browser. Look in the browser&rsquo;s settings for &ldquo;site data&rdquo; or &ldquo;cookies and site data&rdquo;, and remove wiseacresorganic.com.</p>
+        <p>After that, the website forgets your language and your checklist ticks.</p>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="section section-tint" id="ask" aria-labelledby="ask-h">
+      <div class="wrap">
+        <header class="section-head">
+          <p class="hand eyebrow">Still wondering?</p>
+          <h2 id="ask-h">Questions</h2>
+        </header>
+        <p>Questions about this page? Email the farm at <a href="mailto:cathy@wiseacresorganic.com">cathy@wiseacresorganic.com</a>.</p>
+        <p class="fine">This page was written on 4 October 2026, from what the website&rsquo;s code does that day. It is not legal advice. If the website changes, this page may need to change too.</p>
+      </div>
+    </section>
