 | `i18n-facts` | the facts in the translations (no browser, about 5 seconds): every translated text (page text, labels, picture descriptions, texts written by JavaScript) has the same prices, per-person / per-child words, numbers (also written out, also in Devanagari digits), clock times (am / pm matter, the 24-hour clock is the same), dates, months, early / mid / late of a month, days of the week (a range written out is the same set), ages and group sizes ("and up" is not "and under"), units (45 minutes is not 45 hours), e-mail addresses, phone numbers, names and the small words that carry a promise (free, only, always, never, no / not, about, usually, the seasons, the holidays) as its English, in Spanish, Hindi, Chinese and Vietnamese. The meant differences are on `tools/i18n_facts_allow.json`, each with its reason; an entry that matches nothing fails. The reader is tried on wrong translations made on purpose and on a temporary copy of the real lang files with a number, two weekdays, a price and two times changed. `node tools/i18n_facts.mjs` lists every difference with the English next to it |
